  "narrative": {
    "intro": "S Oil obligated $513M in FY26 to date across 19 awards, with an average award size of $27M. Obligations are down 17.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a rise from $340M in FY21 to a peak of $635M in FY24, followed by $624M in FY25 and $513M in FY26. These figures are contract obligations; largest-award and expiring-contract tables use total contract values and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The pattern of annual obligations indicates growth through FY24 and lower obligations so far in FY26. Average award size and award count together show a small number of relatively large awards rather than many small contracts. The downward year-over-year change quantifies the drop in obligations for the current fiscal-year-to-date period compared with the prior year. Use these facts when planning capture efforts or sizing bids for S Oil, and remember that the FY26 total is a partial-year figure.",
